※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=4621

※ Only a value that points into room is made anywhere: a string, a list, a collection, an
※ array of no stated length, a reference, or something holding one.  A number is what it is,
※ wherever it was computed, so saying where it was made says nothing.

fn count(a: &mut arena) → u8 in a:
    0u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let x: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(x)
    if count(&mut x) = 0u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
